/**
 * Orders for any type: Bulk/Bag/Special Products, Road/Train/Road-Train. An order consists of header data (in this table) plus n Order-Items (tlgnc_order_item). For Bulk it is typically n=1, but for rail container orders several bulk items are possible, 1 per container on the rail wagon. For special deliveries such as 'Silostellung', there is one special item + 1 material item. For Bag orders, an order can generally contains more than 1 items. The starting point of an order is always a Shippingpoint (maybe an artificial one), and the end point is always a Shipto. An 'order' is the commercial object for a delivery, the 'assignment' is the logistical object for this. For rail, 'orders' are also used for plain transportation to the railway company.
 */

